## 8. Backtest and symbol-batch research (updated 2026-10-13)

- Engine code: `Blue_engine\backtest\`. It reuses the optimizer's local
  `data\optimizer\ohlcv.sqlite` cache and the existing `optimizer` search-space
  and TPE implementation. No new Python dependency was added; threading,
  multiprocessing, SQLite, and atomic JSON output use the standard library.
- Single backtest contract: a strategy receives `(params, context, bars)` and
  returns a target exposure fraction (or `{"target_position": fraction}`).
  `bars` is a prefix-only view. Decisions execute at the next bar's open;
  equity is marked at each close. Long-only, <=100% exposure is the default.
- Symbol workflow: `run_symbol_batch()` takes the screener's ticker list,
  checks cache window coverage, downloads missing windows in <=365-day chunks
  with bounded threads, then runs per-symbol IS searches in separate processes.
  Workers consume local cached bars only. On Windows, invoke multiprocess use
  from an `if __name__ == "__main__":` guard and provide an importable strategy
  path such as `"my_strategy:signal"` (or another picklable module-level
  callable).
- IS/OOS: the final `oos_fraction` of ordered bars is held out before search.
  A configuration is written under `configurations` only when OOS Sharpe clears
  both `max(0.7 * IS Sharpe, 1.0)` and the OOS deflated-Sharpe probability is at
  least 0.95 using the actual search trial count; OOS max drawdown must be no
  more than 1.3 * IS max drawdown. The absolute Sharpe floor and DSR probability
  are policy assumptions/approximate statistical gates, not guarantees. Missing
  DSR or a trial-count mismatch fails closed. Failures remain under `results`;
  no synthetic fallback is used.
- Output defaults to `data\optimizer\symbol_parameters.json` and is atomically
  replaced. This is a research artifact, **not** the live strategy config.
  Review the report, verify data quality and risk limits, and promote through a
  separately controlled paper/live path; the batch never places orders.
- `LiveMonitor` emits a reason-bearing pause-entry/re-optimization signal for
  drawdown, losing-streak, and rolling-volatility conditions. Its historical
  envelope must declare `baseline_source: "live"` or `"verified_live"`; the
  runner rejects backtest-derived baselines. It is connected
  to the POV runner's child-order boundary only when `live_monitor.enabled`
  is explicitly true. Configure a trusted `provider_ref` (`module:function`)
  and a historical envelope (`max_dd` in percentage points and
  `max_losing_streak`). Before every child order, the guard verifies a
  successful broker positionbook and requires the provider to return finite
  live equity, trade P&L, live daily returns, and at least
  `regime_window + 1` historical daily returns. Missing/unverifiable inputs
  latch the durable kill switch and abort the run. A monitor threshold breach
  pauses new entries while verified exit-phase orders may continue; the trip
  blocks future runs until explicit operator reset. Already-working broker
  orders are not automatically cancelled. Telemetry is sampled on valid quote
  polls at `check_interval_seconds` (default 30) and refreshed again at each
  child-order boundary. A quote-feed outage reaching the configured POV
  `quote_failure_threshold` also latches the kill switch. Durable kill-switch
  storage must be available. Keep
  this feature disabled until the telemetry provider has been validated
  against the broker and the chosen strategy's trade/equity records.
- Provider signature: `provider(client=..., positionbook=...,
  monitor_config=...)`, returning `live_equity`, `live_trade_pnls`,
  `live_daily_returns`, and `historical_daily_returns` sequences. Do not pass
  backtest results as live telemetry. `SlippageReconciler` requires unique,
  explicitly matched long-entry fill IDs, adjusts a copied cost model, and can
  force the same strategy/data to be re-backtested. Persist and review the
  calibrated model before using it in another run.
- Annualization defaults: daily 252, weekly 52, monthly 12; intraday uses a
 375-minute session assumption. These are calendar conventions, not observed
  trading-session counts; holidays, shortened sessions and missing bars can
  change realized periods. Override `periods_per_year` when appropriate and
  inspect the data calendar. `risk_free_per_period` is passed into optimization
  and validation; its default zero is only an explicit assumption, not a current
  RBI rate.
- Optional backtest risk controls: `stop_loss_fraction` and
  `max_daily_loss_fraction` accept fractions in `(0, 1)`. Stops use adverse-first
  OHLC handling: a gap through the stop fills at the worse opening price; an
  intrabar crossing fills at the stop price. Daily loss is measured against the
  first equity mark of the calendar date; after a breach the engine queues a
  flattening order for the next bar and blocks entries for the rest of that date.
  Backtest risk controls are simulation rules, not broker-native guarantees.
